{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983549-condition-based-helth-system-nothing-special-just-a-quirk","id":983549,"title":"Condition Based Helth system (Nothing special - just a quirk)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-07T14:56:57-07:00","id":983549,"title":"Condition Based Helth system (Nothing special - just a quirk)","content":"Those who have read &quot;Blood and Smoke&quot;, is already known that the authors have already proposed a system where health would be expressed as a condition. The conditions were predominantly designed for vampires.<br /> Here I propose a system that could fit all (with certain approximation). Bashing, lethal and aggravate damage remains. Ultimately, the type determines the time of healing.<br /> And so, after all the success remains to injury (lets call it simple DMG for short), we have formed the Wound Condition (it is desirable to clarify, in order to know what type of action we will be imposed a penalty). so, after calculating DMG, we mark a wound condition (or tilt for bashing). We name condition as type of wound: &quot;bruise of left hand&quot; (bashing what placed on arm), &quot;open leg fracture&quot; (for aggravated damage). And in name of condition we mark type of damage (B/L/A). And we mark DMG.<br /> If there mixed type (as ballistic damage, for example), than we should mark both and divide DMG as usual and write down as &quot;arrow in knee L2 B3&quot;. In end of scene we erase bashings.<br /> <br /> How it work?<br /> Each wound condition place penalty (equal to its DMG) on specific action related with wound, AND -1 on any other action.<br /> If DMG bigger than stamina, then we roll stamina (plus any analog of vampyre resilience and +1 for giant if present) without penalty (or -1 for short frame if present... or, if Storyteller is bloodthirsty, with wounds penalty). If there no successes consequences for wound became heavier. In narrative understanding there are maybe death can be present (no one can live with gunshot in the one's head for very long).<br /> Blood loss is auto repeatable condition and trigger stamina check each time storyteller need, if not treated.<br /> <br /> Beat engine.<br /> Once per battle:<br /> when character accumulate 3 wound conditions (conditions, not tilts).<br /> when player roll chance-dice, where penalty present only as wound conditions.<br /> when player rall chance-dice, where penalty present only as one wound condition.<br /> when player voluntarily aggravate effect of wound condition.<br /> In the treatment.<br /> As said, bashings produce only tilts. And any penalty should be erased in the end of scene (or in natural time for type of supernatural being).<br /> Lethal wounds give a beat only when they go the natural way. Work only for mortals and their derivatives.<br /> Aggravated wound give two beats: one for healer and one for patient... Or both for patient, if wound perish in natural way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T19:25:57-07:00","id":985217,"title":"","content":"An optional system for this is coming in Hurt Locker. I'll be interested to see how the different ideas mesh up (or don't).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}